cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in a publication, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "dsgelab: a general toolkit for solving DSGE models in Python"
abstract: >-
  Steady state, Klein/QZ first-order solution, second- and third-order perturbation in Dynare's decision-rule form, Chebyshev projection, time iteration with occasionally binding bounds, value function iteration, the endogenous grid method, Smolyak sparse grids, Tauchen and Rouwenhorst discretisation of processes, Markov regime switching with Kim's filter, heterogeneous agents by the sequence-space Jacobian, perfect foresight with expectation errors, optimal policy (Ramsey, discretion, optimal simple rules) and welfare, Kalman filtering and smoothing with mixed-frequency data, Bayesian estimation (Metropolis-Hastings, SMC, HMC and NUTS) and nonlinear filters, BVAR and DSGE-VAR, local identification, the method of moments, calibration restrictions, global sensitivity, out-of-sample forecast evaluation, shock decompositions and forecasts, Dynare's figures, reading Dynare .mod files, and export to Dynare and MacroModelling.jl. Validated against Dynare, MacroModelling.jl, QuantEcon, dolo, Tasmanian, sequence-jacobian, statsmodels, published solutions and closed forms.
authors:
  - family-names: "Moreira"
    given-names: "Gustavo Hoffmann"
    email: "gustavo@gakusai.net"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0827-2521"
version: "1.0.0rc2"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: MIT
